==Scots==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|sco|broas}}

===Etymology===
Unclear, but possibly deriving from {{der|sco|sco-osc|bruis}}, cognate with {{cog|enm|browes}}, possibly from {{der|sco|fro|broez}}, nominative of {{m|fro|broet||stew, soup made from meat broth}} (modern {{cog|fr|brouet}}) diminutive of {{m|fro|breu}}, from {{der|sco|ML.|brodium}}, from {{der|sco|gem-pro|*bruþą||broth}}. See {{cog|en|broth}}.

===Noun===
{{sco-noun}}

# A dish of meal (usually {{l|sco|oatmeal}}, sometimes {{l|sco|peasemeal}}, {{l|sco|beremeal}}, or a combination of meals) made with boiling water or hot milk, which sometimes includes additions such as salt, skimmed fat from broth, or {{l|sco|kail}}.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|sco|birse-brose}} (brose with whisky added as an ingredient)
* {{l|sco|brose-bicker}} (a wooden vessel for brose)
* {{l|sco|kail-brose}} (brose with kail added)
* {{l|sco|querny-brose}} (brose made from roughly-ground meal)

